        "Most of the essays in this collection address specific themes and problems in the context of the Grundlage, such as imagination, time, representation, reflection, deduction, and transcendental methodology. Others examine the relationship of Fichte's philosophy to Kant's and the influence of the Grundlage upon such philosophers as Jacobi, Schelling, and Hegel.",
        "Collectively, these essays constitute an ideal introduction to the reading of Fichte's notoriously difficult but deeply rewarding work."
